{"availability":"available","full":"mohamedaminefezzani/rag-debugger","name":"rag-debugger","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-13T16:15:05Z","updated":"2026-10-01T16:37:40Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Intercept, inspect, and fix your RAG retrieval pipeline.","Most RAG bugs aren't in your code, they're in your retrieval. Wrong chunks get selected, knowledge gaps go undetected, and you find out when users complain. rag-debugger gives you visibility into exactly what your vector DB returned, why it won, and what's missing from your knowledge base.","A query like \"cancel my iOS subscription and get a refund\" is really four questions. Standard RAG scores the whole query — if cancellation chunks score high, the query looks covered. rag-debugger decomposes it into atomic sub-intents and scores each one independently, so a missing refund policy is always caught even when the cancellation docs are excellent."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mohamedaminefezzani/rag-debugger/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a9977a2ac5dd958494c78615f2c5a162ca7cc6f4e9b95bf30a5e465a6e51a513","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Intercept, inspect, and fix your RAG retrieval pipeline.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mohamedaminefezzani/rag-debugger/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a9977a2ac5dd958494c78615f2c5a162ca7cc6f4e9b95bf30a